# Git — autonomous commit & push

The owner delegated commit/push decisions to the agent for this repo.

## When to commit and push

Do both **without asking** when:

- A bounded task is complete (feature, docs, audit slice, fix verified)
- User says **go**, **yes**, **ship it**, **commit**, or equivalent
- Build/typecheck passes for code changes (or failure is documented in commit if intentional WIP branch)

## Safety (non-negotiable)

- **Never** commit `.env`, credentials, Firebase keys, API secrets, or `*adminsdk*.json`
- **Never** `git push --force` to main/master; warn on any force push
- **Never** amend unless HEAD was created this session and not pushed
- **Never** skip hooks unless user explicitly requests
- **Never** update git config

## Commit message

- 1–2 sentences, focus on **why**
- Use HEREDOC for formatting

## Push

- Push current branch after successful commit
- Use `-u origin HEAD` if branch has no upstream
- Report commit hash + branch + remote URL when done

## When to still ask

- Destructive git operations (hard reset, force push, mass delete)
- Ambiguous scope with large unrelated dirty files
- Commit would include suspected secrets

